{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00WU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}_{i\\in I} \\in \\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\to V$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$u(T \\times_V V_i) \\to u(T) \\times_{u(V)} u(V_i)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-continuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:11cdc8f111c7ab00426d44504141b1f603677dc498a6d4ee5f860b307731fe4c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4bb652280454d50c48f5c8a4f20dca516c332a4b322cd764d24e0d58edcc4485", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites.\nA functor <MATH_0003> is called\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>continuous<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every\n<MATH_0004>\nwe have the following\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is in <MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for any morphism <MATH_0007> in <MATH_0008> the morphism\n<MATH_0009> is an isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3379b84264c9e1ebcb514e937809351444cc17e993f749a51bb1dda56b2a31d5", "unit_id": "tag:00WV:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$u^p\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} \\circ u$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nu^p\\mathcal{F} (V) = \\mathcal{F}(u(V))\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$V$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:55c48ad7a4f9ea4c07b9f4b56883742aff70b0b613c170b16c4caf20b023ead2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88ca6576859bd38baf7e019187131642a1b2540121b70ffaaf46b81c461036c5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that given a functor <MATH_0001> as above, and a presheaf of sets\n<MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003> we have defined\n<MATH_0004> to be simply the presheaf\n<MATH_0005>, in other words\n<MATH_0006>\nfor every object <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:216dcc8f96e73cc0a2f87dbe1f7718df161f8d7458092894547c8e0119036d13", "unit_id": "tag:00WU:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00WU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0006": "$u^p\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushforward-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9c9646db093f563c3bc7b92a7d04b67d07c76f1be748f624dca458ae182f2183", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf53575d0eb4f59eb00d93f97e39dbe770c19a3afa47acfa5d2da3d43bd1bae5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a continuous functor.\nIf <MATH_0004> is a sheaf on <MATH_0005> then\n<MATH_0006> is a sheaf as well.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a5013b43a331af3b4a97917b5e55837c708b1528db92fb9c6ef1e7a13456c562", "unit_id": "tag:00WW:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00WU", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$u(V_i \\times_V V_j) =\nu(V_i)\\times_{u(V)}u(V_j)$", "MATH_0005": "$u^p\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4591f2551f17e2a775ce009dc6a80af4bd2a4b4409a9b783db846de2289877e8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:424e3d03144c7f0b9275badf58494e188e67684f76e67b542f3347a07f5e694d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a covering.\nBy assumption <MATH_0002> is a covering\nin <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>. Hence the sheaf condition for\n<MATH_0005> and the covering <MATH_0006>\nis precisely the same as the sheaf condition for <MATH_0007>\nand the covering <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fcbcdf95724a3cd09715f13b2200cfc8f194e41203a01a68ae32367189012f1", "unit_id": "tag:00WW:proof"}
