{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "00WU", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\v C", "ACCENT_0002": "\\v C", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPCLOSE_0002": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "GROUPOPEN_0002": "{", "ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMCLOSE_0002": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "ITEMOPEN_0002": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V_i \\to V\\}_{i\\in I} \\in \\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\to V$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$u(T \\times_V V_i) \\to u(T) \\times_{u(V)} u(V_i)$", "MATH_0011": "$u$", "MATH_0012": "$u(V_i) \\to u(V)$", "MATH_0013": "$u(\\mathcal{V}) = \\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0014": "$H^0(u(\\mathcal{V}), \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_j \\to u(V)\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\text{Cov}(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0019": "$\\{u(V_i) \\to u(V)\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0020": "$u(\\mathcal{V})$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0022": "$H^0(u(\\mathcal{V}), \\mathcal{F}) = H^0(\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{F}(u(V)) = H^0(u(\\mathcal{V}), \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0025": "$u^p\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0027": "$H^0(\\mathcal{V}, u^p\\mathcal{F}) =\nH^0(u(\\mathcal{V}), \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{F}(u(V)) = u^p\\mathcal{F}(V)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-combinatorial-tautological}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-sheaf}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-sheaves}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{remark-both-refine-same-H0}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-sheaf}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-sheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-quasi-continuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:448ce452c3899c3e434a85e80514769d0aac073b54fa2826846e743ada2c9301", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9f9b8ab19a50880368e660b4e0e55d0220706371892e3d4a537847a6fe8edc8", "source_text": "(Skip on first reading.)\nLet <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites. Let us\nuse the definition of tautologically equivalent families of maps,\nsee Definition <REF_0001>\nto (slightly) weaken the conditions defining continuity.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a functor.\nLet us call <MATH_0004> <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-continuous<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every\n<MATH_0005>\nwe have the following\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(1')<ITEMCLOSE_0001> the family of maps\n<MATH_0006> is tautologically equivalent\nto an element of <MATH_0007>, and\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(2)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> for any morphism <MATH_0008> in <MATH_0009> the morphism\n<MATH_0010> is an isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0002>\nWe are going to see that Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003> hold in case\n<MATH_0011> is quasi-continuous as well.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nWe first remark that the morphisms <MATH_0012> are representable, since\nthey are isomorphic to representable morphisms (by the first condition).\nIn particular, the family <MATH_0013>\ngives rise to a zeroth <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech cohomology group\n<MATH_0014> for any presheaf <MATH_0015> on\n<MATH_0016>.\nLet <MATH_0017> be an element\nof <MATH_0018> tautologically\nequivalent to <MATH_0019>. Note that <MATH_0020>\nis a refinement of <MATH_0021> and vice versa. Hence by Remark\n<REF_0004> we see that\n<MATH_0022>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0023> is a sheaf, then\n<MATH_0024> because\nof the sheaf property expressed in terms of zeroth <GROUPOPEN_0002><ACCENT_0002><GROUPCLOSE_0002>ech cohomology\ngroups. We conclude that <MATH_0025> is a sheaf if <MATH_0026>\nis a sheaf, since <MATH_0027> which we just observed is\nequal to <MATH_0028>. Thus Lemma\n<REF_0005> holds. Lemma <REF_0006>\nfollows immediately.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:44bd9d3a1bea3c36521564e4fdc5a28ac5482ad02c721a6d3c3dd14b95ec77ad", "unit_id": "tag:00WZ:statement"}
